# Garbage collection in one breath

## Garbage = unreachable — from **GC roots** (stack locals, statics), follow every reference; reachable = live

```java
var user = new User("Ana");   // reachable
user = null;                  // now unreachable → collectible
```

Reachability, **not** "will I use it" — a held reference you never touch stays alive. That gap causes most leaks.

## Generational hypothesis — most objects die young

- **Young gen** — new objects, **minor GC** small/frequent/fast · survivors **promoted** to **old gen** (rare **major GC**)

## Collectors (pick with a flag)

**G1** (default) · **Parallel** (throughput) · **ZGC / Shenandoah** (low-pause, concurrent). Tradeoff is the **stop-the-world pause**.

## What you do

- **Don't** call `System.gc()` (a hint; forces a costly full GC) · **Do** avoid leaks — growing statics, caches, listeners · one knob: `-Xmx`
